\paragraph{Component decomposition (fixed-$K$ analysis).}
\looseness=-2 The remaining rows of Table~\ref{tab:main} are analysis baselines at fixed $K$, not proposed methods. CRM obs\_only at $K{=}10$ reaches $16.8 \pm 1.8$\% on Object ($p{=}0.003$) and $34.4 \pm 1.5$\% on Spatial. Random selection fails to exceed VLA-only on either benchmark (Object $9.7$\% vs.\ $11.0$\%; Spatial $29.3$\% vs.\ $29.3$\%), confirming that sampling more actions without ranking is insufficient; argmin adds $+$1.3\,pp, and CRM correction contributes $+$4.5\,pp (78\% of the gain). At $K{=}5$, correction contributes 55\%. At $K{=}1$, correction without centering falls below baseline ($10.3$\%), validating the $K{\geq}2$ requirement.

